<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cumnock slips to net loss for year.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cumnock slips to net loss for year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		loss 0.61 vs profit 1.34</p>
<p>    Net				 loss 0.03 vs profit 1.42</p>
<p>    Sales				   77.17 vs 57.92</p>
<p>    Other income			   2.65 vs 0.75</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     n/a vs 7.2</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			 1.21 vs 0.16</p>
<p>    Tax					0.63 vs 0.08</p>
<p>    Interest				 1.42 vs 0.83</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   2.74 vs 1.55</p>
<p>NOTE: Cumnock Coal Ltd is a coal miner and is about 25.14 percent owned by Swiss metals house Glencore International AG. CIM Resources holds about 5.01 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
